<table class="messages">
 <tr><th colspan="4" class="header">Messages (4)</th></tr>
 
  <tr>
    <th>
     <a href="#msg366938" id="msg366938">msg366938</a> - <a
    href="msg366938">(view)</a></th>
   <th>Author: Brandt Bucher (brandtbucher) <span title="Contributor form received">*</span> <img src="@@file/committer.png" title="Python committer" alt="(Python committer)" /></th>
   <th>Date: 2020-04-21 19:59</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
   <td colspan="4" class="content">
    
    <pre>There are several places in the ast module where the use of zip is allowing malformed nodes to have unpaired children silently thrown away. A couple of short examples:

&gt;&gt;&gt; from ast import Constant, Dict, literal_eval, unparse
&gt;&gt;&gt; nasty_dict = Dict(keys=[Constant("I don't have a value!")], values=[])
&gt;&gt;&gt; unparse(nasty_dict)
'{}'
&gt;&gt;&gt; literal_eval(nasty_dict)
{}

I'm currently working on a patch to raise errors instead.</pre>
   </td>
  </tr>
 
 
  <tr>
    <th>
     <a href="#msg366941" id="msg366941">msg366941</a> - <a
    href="msg366941">(view)</a></th>
   <th>Author: Batuhan Taskaya (BTaskaya) <span title="Contributor form received">*</span> <img src="@@file/committer.png" title="Python committer" alt="(Python committer)" /></th>
   <th>Date: 2020-04-21 21:03</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
   <td colspan="4" class="content">
    
    <pre>See <a href="https://bugs.python.org/msg360767">https://bugs.python.org/msg360767</a> for ast.unparse's point of view regarding malformed nodes.</pre>
   </td>
  </tr>
 
 
  <tr>
    <th>
     <a href="#msg368200" id="msg368200">msg368200</a> - <a
    href="msg368200">(view)</a></th>
   <th>Author: Pablo Galindo Salgado (pablogsal) <span title="Contributor form received">*</span> <img src="@@file/committer.png" title="Python committer" alt="(Python committer)" /></th>
